  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="4cfa-37e6-d58c-90f1" name="Libyan (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #106 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The tribes of North Africa were the original inhabitants of the Nile delta region and kin to the Egyptians. They were both a constant nuisance and a source of mercenaries to the Egyptian Pharaohs. They posed the greatest danger when acting in concert with the Sea Peoples, and The New Kingdom fought three major wars against them. Eventually one of the most warlike tribes, the Meshwesh, was resettled in the Nile delta by agreement to provide a stable source of mercenary troops. Allies And Mercenaries: The army may take allies from the Hyksos or Sea Peoples lists, but not both at the same time.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Libyan]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: up to 15%
  Infantry: at least 35%
  Characters: up to 25% Chariotry: up to 15% Infantry: At least 35% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
